error[E0521]: borrowed data escapes outside of closure
  --> tests/hook_compile_fail/keeps_a_lent_reference.rs:17:46
   |
15 |             let kept = Arc::clone(&kept);
   |                 ---- `kept` declared here, outside of the closure body
16 |             Box::pin(async move {
17 |                 args.with(0, |text: &String| kept.lock().unwrap().push(text));
   |                               ----           ^^^^^^^^^^^ `text` escapes the closure body here
   |                               |
   |                               `text` is a reference that is only valid in the closure body
   |
   = note: requirement occurs because of the type `std::sync::Mutex<Vec<&std::string::String>>`, which makes the generic argument `Vec<&std::string::String>` invariant
   = note: the struct `std::sync::Mutex<T>` is invariant over the parameter `T`
   = help: see <https://doc.rust-lang.org/nomicon/subtyping.html> for more information about variance
